REM ============================================================
REM project.conf - copy this file to project.conf (drop .example)
REM and fill in your values for this specific project.
REM
REM project.conf is GITIGNORED - never committed, never pushed,
REM never uploaded by FTP. It only ever lives on your machine.
REM
REM Nothing in this file is a secret. FTP password, FTP username,
REM Supabase URL, Supabase keys, and any Supabase service-role key
REM live ONLY as GitHub Actions repo secrets (set once via GitHub's
REM web UI - see docs/NEW-PROJECT.md) and never appear here or in
REM git history.
REM
REM If you run deploy.bat without filling this in first, it will
REM ask you for anything missing and save your answers back into
REM this file - you only get asked once per value.
REM ============================================================

REM --- Identity ---

REM Full display name, shown in page titles, sidebar brand, login
REM screen, etc. e.g. Acme Risk Register
APP_NAME=ionetiq Template

REM Short code - lowercase, no spaces. Used as: the prefix on every
REM build zip Claude names for you (e.g. PROJECT_CODE=acme means
REM zips are named acme_DDMMYYYY_HHmm.zip), and the FTP folder name
REM (public_html/PROJECT_CODE/).
PROJECT_CODE=template

REM Which version of the template (see TEMPLATE-VERSION.txt and
REM docs/TEMPLATE-CHANGELOG.md in the template repo) this project was
REM originally created from. Set once, at project creation, and never
REM changed afterward - it's a historical record, not something that
REM auto-updates. Used when deciding whether/what to pull in from a
REM newer template version later - see docs/UPDATING-PROJECTS.md.
TEMPLATE_VERSION_AT_CREATION=1.1.0

REM Shown in page footers, e.g. ionetiq
COMPANY_NAME=ionetiq

REM --- Local paths ---

REM Where Claude's build zips land when you save them. Leave blank
REM to default to your Windows Downloads folder.
DOWNLOADS_DIR=C:\Users\mikeb\My Drive\Downloads

REM This project's working directory - where deploy.bat actually
REM lives and runs from. Leave blank to default to the directory
REM deploy.bat is currently running in (the normal case - you would
REM only set this if you run deploy.bat from somewhere else and
REM point it at a working directory elsewhere).
WORKING_DIR=C:\inetpub\wwwroot\Template

REM --- GitHub ---

REM e.g. https://github.com/ionetiqdev/acme-risk.git
GITHUB_REPO_URL=https://github.com/ionetiqdev/ionetiq-template.git

REM --- Supabase / FTP ---

REM Just a reference name so Claude and deploy.bat's reminders can refer
REM to "your Supabase project" by name in messages - this is NOT used to
REM connect to anything and is not a secret, just a label, e.g. acme-risk
SUPABASE_PROJECT_NAME=template

REM Nothing else Supabase/FTP-related lives here. They're set ONCE per
REM repo as GitHub Actions secrets via GitHub's web UI (Settings >
REM Secrets and variables > Actions). See docs/NEW-PROJECT.md for the
REM exact steps. The required secret names are:
REM   SUPABASE_URL
REM   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
REM   FTP_HOST
REM   FTP_USERNAME
REM   FTP_PASSWORD
REM   SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL          (optional - omit to skip Slack notify)
REM
REM deploy.bat will remind you these need to be set in GitHub the
REM first time you run it for a new project, and won't ask you to
REM type them here.
